3.  **`preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]+/', '-', ...)`**:
    *   Input: `"un titulo en espanol con n y acentos!"`
    *   The regex finds any sequence of characters that are not `a-z` or `0-9`.
    *   It finds the spaces (` `) and the exclamation mark (`!`).
    *   Each sequence of these "bad" characters is replaced by a single hyphen.
    *   Output: `"un-titulo-en-espanol-con-n-y-acentos-"`

4.  **`trim(..., '-')`**:
    *   Input: `"un-titulo-en-espanol-con-n-y-acentos-"`
    *   It removes the hyphen from the end of the string.
